  "goodToKnow": "Die Prosa is prose, writing without verse: Romane, Erzählungen, Kurzgeschichten. The opposite is die Lyrik (poetry) or Poesie. Kafka, Thomas Mann and Christa Wolf are masters of German prose. Prosaisch means prosaic or matter-of-fact: eine prosaische Erklärung. German school literature divides texts into Lyrik, Epik (narrative) and Dramatik. It has no plural."
